<title>FRANCE: Juppe to press case for stronger dollar at G7.</title>
<headline>Juppe to press case for stronger dollar at G7.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe said on Wednesday he would ask the Group of Seven (G7) to take up the issue of what he said was the dollar's weakness.</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar is clearly undervalued...and therefore it is right for the French government to ask its partners that this question be raised in the relevant international fora, notably the G7, which is the place where these problems of currency parity must be dealt with as they have in the past,&quot; Juppe said during a speech to parliament.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
